{
  "_comment": "Reference entry to merge into C:\\Users\\jesus\\.minimax\\mcp\\mcp.json. The actual installer (infra/install.sh) does this automatically; this file is documentation only.",
  "bash-mcp": {
    "url": "http://<WSL_IP>:54321/mcp/",
    "type": "streamable-http",
    "enabled": true,
    "configured": true,
    "description": "WSL bash executor \u2014 REQUIRED for any WSL command. Tools (v0.7): bash-mcp_run_command, bash-mcp_check_env, bash-mcp_list_binaries, bash-mcp_which, bash-mcp_status, bash-mcp_classify, bash-mcp_session_create, bash-mcp_session_run, bash-mcp_session_destroy, bash-mcp_session_list. DO NOT use `wsl -d ... -- bash -c \"...\"` from PowerShell \u2014 that path has quoting, UTF-16, and PATH bugs. Instead, call bash-mcp_run_command({command: \"...\"}). Safety: denylist (HARD + SOFT) + timeouts + output cap + audit log; pass dangerous=true to bypass SOFT denylist (HARD cannot be bypassed). Sessions: server-side cwd + env persistence across calls; process-lifetime only \u2014 destroy explicitly to free. v0.7 opt-in: bash-mcp_classify for self-check; BASH_MCP_SESSION_IDLE_TIMEOUT_S for session auto-eviction; BASH_MCP_AUDIT_GZIP_THRESHOLD_BYTES for gzip-on-rotation."
  }
}
